---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Eric Carlisle's website uses analytics, handles contact-form submissions, and protects the contact form from automated abuse."
  pageType="privacy"
>
  <p><em>Effective August 20, 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    This policy explains what information this website collects, why it is used, and the choices
    available to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Website analytics</h2>

  <p>
    This site uses Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site. Its standard
    measurement can collect information such as pages viewed, session activity, approximate
    location, browser type, and device type. Google Analytics uses a first-party cookie named
    <code>_ga</code> to distinguish visitors and sessions.
  </p>

  <p>
    This information is used to understand the site&rsquo;s audience and improve its content and
    experience. The site does not intentionally send names, email addresses, or contact-form
    contents to Google Analytics. Learn more about{' '}<a
      href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11593727?hl=en"
    >Google Analytics data collection</a>{' '}and read{' '}<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
    >Google&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact-form submissions</h2>

  <p>
    When you use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, the site collects the name, email
    address, subject, and message you provide. That information is used to deliver your message and
    respond to your inquiry. Please do not submit sensitive personal information through the form.
  </p>

  <p>
    Contact submissions are processed by a Cloudflare Worker and delivered to the site owner by
    email through Resend. The site code does not write contact messages to a separate application
    database. Messages may remain in the site owner&rsquo;s inbox and the email provider&rsquo;s systems as
    needed to respond to and manage the inquiry.
  </p>

  <h2>Spam and bot protection</h2>

  <p>
    The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to help prevent spam and automated submissions.
    Turnstile runs browser-based security challenges and processes limited browser, device, and
    network signals needed to distinguish people from automated traffic. The contact-form service
    also uses the connecting IP address for short-term rate limiting and sends it to Cloudflare with
    the Turnstile verification token.
  </p>

  <p>
    Cloudflare states that Turnstile does not access, store, or transmit form entries or other page
    inputs. Learn more in the{' '}<a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/"
    >Cloudflare Turnstile documentation</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and your choices</h2>

  <p>
    Cookies are small text files that a website or service can place in your browser. This site uses
    Google Analytics measurement, including its first-party analytics cookie. You can control or
    delete cookies through your browser settings. Disabling analytics cookies may reduce the
    accuracy of site-usage measurement.
  </p>

  <p>
    Google also provides a{' '}<a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
    >Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How information is used</h2>

  <p>Information described on this page is used to:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Measure site usage and improve the site&rsquo;s content and experience.</li>
    <li>Deliver and respond to contact-form submissions.</li>
    <li>Protect the contact form from spam, bots, and abusive automated activity.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>

  <p>
    Google Analytics, Cloudflare Turnstile, and Resend are service providers used for the site
    functions described above. Their handling of information is also governed by their own terms
    and privacy policies. Information may also be disclosed when required by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

  <p>
    This policy may be updated when the site&rsquo;s data practices or services change. The effective
    date at the top of the page will be revised when an update is published.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy questions</h2>

  <p>
    For privacy questions or requests, contact Eric Carlisle through the{' '}<a href="/contact/"
    >contact form</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
